+# Behavioral evals: release-notes
+
+Run each prompt in a fresh agent session against a Quillnote checkout, or a fixture repo with the described PRs. Compare what the agent does with the expected behavior. Cases 5–7 are regression tests for mistakes that happened when the notes were written by hand.
+
+## 1. Direct request
+Prompt: "It's Friday, write the release notes."
+Trigger: yes.
+Expected: runs `scripts/collect_prs.py`, states the date range and whether labels came from GitHub, filters and groups the PRs, writes `release-notes/<today>.md`, and lists the excluded PRs.
+Disallowed: asking for the date range when earlier notes exist; committing or pushing.
+
+## 2. Paraphrase
+Prompt: "Can you put together what we shipped to customers this week?"
+Trigger: yes. Expected: same as case 1.
+
+## 3. Near miss
+Prompt: "Summarize this week's merged PRs for the eng standup."
+Trigger: no. This is an internal audience, so refactors and chores are relevant and no notes file should be written.
+
+## 4. Empty week
+Fixture: only PRs titled `chore: bump deps`, `test: add importer tests`, and `refactor: split sync module`.
+Expected: the file contains exactly `Small fixes and performance work this week.` and the report lists all three exclusions.
+
+## 5. Regression: an exciting refactor title
+Fixture: a PR labeled `refactor` and titled "Brand new sync engine".
+Expected: excluded. The report names it as excluded because of its `refactor` label.
+
+## 6. Regression: a `fix:` PR that adds behavior
+Fixture: `fix: allow exporting archived notes`. Archived notes could never be exported before.
+Expected: listed under New, for example "You can now export archived notes", not under Fixed.
+
+## 7. Regression: platform tag
+Fixture: `fix: crash when rotating editor`, which only changes `ios/**/*.swift`, and `feat: keyboard shortcuts`, which only changes `web/**`.
+Expected: the first is `[iOS]` under Fixed and the second is `[Web]` under New.
+
+## 8. Privacy leaks
+Fixture: merge subject `Merge pull request #88 from priya/QN-412-acme-export`, body "Fix Acme Corp export timeout (QN-412)".
+Expected: the item reads like "Large exports no longer time out." It contains no "Priya", "Acme", "QN-412", or "#88".
+
+## 9. Word limit
+Fixture: 25 customer-facing PRs.
+Expected: related items are merged until the file is under 200 words, as measured with `wc -w`, and the report names anything left out.
+
+## 10. GitHub CLI unavailable
+Setup: `gh` is missing or not logged in.
+Expected: the agent uses the script's git fallback, infers categories from title prefixes and files, and says that labels were not checked.
+Disallowed: claiming that labels were checked.
+
+## 11. Re-run on the same day
+Setup: `release-notes/<today>.md` already exists.
+Expected: the same range is used (today's note is ignored), the agent shows a diff, and it asks before overwriting.
+
+## 12. Range named by the user
+Prompt: "We skipped last week. Do notes covering the last two weeks."
+Expected: the agent passes `--since` with the date two weeks back and states that range.
